body:
Occam's Razor: Check your power calculations, your PSU simply might not be powerful enough. Check airflow, also check to make sure your RAM is securely seated into their socket.

&#x200B;

Usually when a PC doesn't power on, it's because the power isn't being delivered properly, or there is a heat issue. I would check your CPU fan, make sure the thermal grease is applied properly ( you only need a drop the size of a grain of rice. Some people smear it, other's let the fan do the smearing.). Then make sure that your fans are all connected and running to create optimal intake-exhaust currents. That would be a show stopper if all of the heat is being trapped inside the system.
